/* =============================================================================
 * LINKER ENCRYPTION CONSTANTS
 * ============================================================================= */

/**
 * Number of Poseidon-cipher ciphertexts produced per UTXO leaf for the linker.
 *
 * @remarks
 * For each leaf the six plaintexts are:
 * - `senderAddressLow`   (lower 128 bits of the sender's address)
 * - `senderAddressHigh`  (upper 128 bits)
 * - `amount`             (token quantity for this leaf)
 * - `mintAddressLow`     (lower 128 bits of the mint address)
 * - `mintAddressHigh`    (upper 128 bits)
 * - `leafCommitment`     (Poseidon commitment for this UTXO)
 *
 * Each of these is encrypted under the Transaction Viewing Key (TVK) using the Poseidon
 * cipher so that the holder of the TVK can reconstruct the transaction details for auditing
 * without learning the receiver's identity.
 * @internal
 */
const LINKER_ENCRYPTIONS_PER_LEAF = 6;

/**
 * Domain separator used when deriving per-linker-element keystream blinding factors.
 *
 * @remarks
 * A unique blinding factor is produced for every (leaf, keyIndex) pair using KMAC256 with
 * this domain and the `claimModifiedGenerationIndex` as the key material:
 * ```
 * blindingFactorOffset = KMAC256(
 *   key   = LINKER_KEYSTREAM_BLINDING_FACTOR_DOMAIN + globalKeyIndex,
 *   data  = claimModifiedGenerationIndex (32-byte BE),
 * )
 * ```
 * The resulting blinding factor is then passed to `keystreamCommitmentGenerator` so the
 * circuit can verify each keystream element without re-computing the Poseidon cipher.
 * @internal
 */
const LINKER_KEYSTREAM_BLINDING_FACTOR_DOMAIN =
  "receiverClaimUtxoToEta / linkerKeystreamBlindingFactor";

/* =============================================================================
 * RESCUE CIPHER CONSTANTS
 * ============================================================================= */

/**
 * Total number of Rescue-prime cipher encryptions performed per batch.
 *
 * @remarks
 * The seven encrypted values are, in order:
 * 1. `finalAmount`         — token amount credited to the receiver after all fees
 * 2. `protocolFees`        — deducted protocol commission
 * 3. `relayerFees`         — deducted relayer commission
 * 4. `mvkLow`              — lower 128 bits of the receiver's master viewing key
 * 5. `mvkHigh`             — upper 128 bits of the master viewing key
 * 6. `randomFactorLow`     — lower 128 bits of the polynomial commitment random factor
 * 7. `randomFactorHigh`    — upper 128 bits of the polynomial commitment random factor
 *
 * These ciphertexts are stored in the proof PDA so the MXE network can decrypt them (using
 * the receiver's X25519 key) and credit the receiver's encrypted balance during the MPC
 * callback without learning any identifying information.
 * @internal
 */
const RESCUE_ENCRYPTIONS_COUNT = 7;

/**
 * Domain separator for deriving the random polynomial commitment factor.
 *
 * @remarks
 * The random factor `r` is drawn from the Curve25519 field and is used as the constant
 * term of the polynomial evaluated at the Fiat-Shamir challenge point:
 * ```
 * p(x) = finalAmount + protocolFees*x + relayerFees*x^2 + mvkLow*x^3 + mvkHigh*x^4 + r*x^5
 * ```
 * Deriving `r` deterministically from the `claimModifiedGenerationIndex` ensures that the
 * proof is reproducible for the same UTXO batch while remaining unpredictable to an
 * observer who does not know the master seed.
 * @internal
 */
const RANDOM_FACTOR_FOR_POLYNOMIAL_COMMITMENT_DOMAIN =
  "receiverClaimUtxoToEta / randomFactorForPolynomialCommitment";

/**
 * Domain separator for deriving the Rescue encryption commitment blinding factor.
 *
 * @remarks
 * The blinding factor is derived using a 512-bit KMAC256 output (reduced into BN254)
 * so that the resulting blinding factor is uniformly distributed over the BN254 scalar
 * field.  It is used by `rescueEncryptionCommitmentGenerator` to produce a hiding
 * commitment over all seven ciphertexts, preventing an observer from correlating
 * multiple claims from the same receiver.
 * @internal
 */
const RESCUE_ENCRYPTION_COMMITMENT_BLINDING_FACTOR_DOMAIN =
  "receiverClaimUtxoToEta / rescueEncryptionCommitmentBlindingFactor";

/**
 * Output byte length requested from KMAC256 when a 512-bit value is needed.
 *
 * @remarks
 * A 512-bit output is used when sampling a BN254 field element via rejection-free reduction
 * ({@link bn254FieldElementSampler}) — twice the field size ensures the bias is
 * negligible (< 2^{-128}).
 * @internal
 */
const KMAC_512_OUTPUT_LENGTH = 64;

/**
 * Number of BN254 field elements that make up the public aggregated hash input.
 *
 * @remarks
 * The 70-element array fed to `poseidonAggregator` is the sole public input to the
 * Groth16 verifier.  The index layout is documented in Section 17 of `processUtxoInBatch`:
 *
 * - [0]      Merkle root
 * - [1-2]    Mint address (low, high)
 * - [3-6]    Protocol fee parameters (base, lower bound, upper bound, bps)
 * - [7-10]   Relayer fee parameters (base, lower bound, upper bound, bps)
 * - [11-25]  Fiat-Shamir challenge and its powers 2–5, each as 3 Base-85 limbs
 * - [26-46]  Seven Rescue ciphertexts, each as 3 Base-85 limbs
 * - [47]     Rescue encryption commitment
 * - [48-50]  Polynomial evaluation result (3 limbs)
 * - [51-52]  Relayer public key (low, high)
 * - [53-54]  Receiver destination address (low, high)
 * - [55]     Linker encryptions aggregated Poseidon hash
 * - [56]     Linker keystream commitments aggregated Poseidon hash
 * - [57]     Nullifier hashes aggregated Poseidon hash
 * - [58]     Total relayer fixed SOL fees
 * - [59-60]  Ephemeral signer address (low, high)
 * - [61-66]  TVK timestamp (year, month, day, hour, minute, second)
 * - [67-68]  Receiver's X25519 public key / arcisPublicKey (low, high)
 * - [69]     Rescue encryption nonce
 * @internal
 */
const AGGREGATED_HASH_INPUT_COUNT = 64;

